   "name": "Pete",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s6",
   "summary": "First mention: “When Thornton’s partners, Hans and Pete, arrived on the long-expected raft, Buck refused to notice them till he learned they were close to Thornton; after that he tolerated them in a passive sort of way, accepting fav…”"
  },
  {
   "id": "billee",
   "name": "Billee",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s2",
   "summary": "First mention: ““Billee” and “Joe” he called them, two brothers, and true huskies both.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "curly",
   "name": "Curly",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s1",
   "summary": "First mention: “Buck saw money pass between them, and was not surprised when Curly, a good-natured Newfoundland, and he were led away by the little weazened man.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "joe",
   "name": "Joe",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s2",
   "summary": "First mention: ““Billee” and “Joe” he called them, two brothers, and true huskies both.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "matthewson",
   "name": "Matthewson",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s6",
   "summary": "First mention: “and walk off with it for a hundred yards?” demanded Matthewson, a Bonanza King, he of the seven hundred vaunt.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "manuel",
   "name": "Manuel",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s1",
   "summary": "First mention: “But Buck did not read the newspapers, and he did not know that Manuel, one of the gardener’s helpers, was an undesirable acquaintance.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "southland",
   "name": "Southland",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s1",
   "summary": "First mention: “That was the last he saw of the man in the red sweater, and as Curly and he looked at receding Seattle from the deck of the _Narwhal_, it was the last he saw of the warm Southland.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "dub",
   "name": "Dub",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s2",
   "summary": "First mention: “A great uproar was raised, but he was unsuspected; while Dub, an awkward blunderer who was always getting caught, was punished for Buck’s misdeed.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "skeet",
   "name": "Skeet",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s6",
   "summary": "First mention: “For that matter, they were all loafing,—Buck, John Thornton, and Skeet and Nig,—waiting for the raft to come that was to carry them down to Dawson.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "nig",
   "name": "Nig",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s6",
   "summary": "First mention: “For that matter, they were all loafing,—Buck, John Thornton, and Skeet and Nig,—waiting for the raft to come that was to carry them down to Dawson.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "northland",
   "name": "Northland",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s1",
   "summary": "First mention: “Because men, groping in the Arctic darkness, had found a yellow metal, and because steamship and transportation companies were booming the find, thousands of men were rushing into the Northland.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "teek",
   "name": "Teek",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s4",
   "summary": "First mention: “At the Rink Rapids two native huskies, Teek and Koona, were added; and the celerity with which Buck broke them in took away François’s breath.”"
  }
